mmit 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-pr"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 371766, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01R9crqspcJW7r4cSRyvkvfE", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-pr", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 371766, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01R9crqspcJW7r4cSRyvkvfE", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 373333, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "The nightly build failure is fixed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, though its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding. That made `2.665` round to `2.67` instead of `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/banker-rounding-fin-212`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner, so that still has to happen through the normal review process.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the source and the test to see what's expected.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01MZaHVk2PdHe1dvRFvwFZGA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TsMazCjDnJT3xhyFt6MyfU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0143mq7UngK7vFKfrzoiriyL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `src/money.py` uses `ROUND_HALF_UP` while its docstring and the test both call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. With HALF_UP, `2.665` rounds to `2.67`, which fails the test. I'll create a branch and make the one-line fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0193wZRJHTgVsA6F9hNJLLV1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0128BaF75szS4jhEePLuNzPq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)\n\nround_money's docstring specifies banker's rounding per FIN-212, but the\nimplementation used ROUND_HALF_UP. Switch to ROUND_HALF_EVEN so that\ntests/test_money.py passes (e.g. 2.665 -> 2.66).", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CcS1wXn2iN6HYWrXUDEPBa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-fix-ci"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AvPXRX2mtAbBi9RSw7thJm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on the branch. Next I'll open the pull request against main with alex as reviewer. I won't merge it, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01R9crqspcJW7r4cSRyvkvfE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "Fixes the nightly build failure in tests/test_money.py.\n\n`round_money` documents banker's rounding per FIN-212, but the implementation used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, so `Decimal(\"2.665\")` rounded to `2.67` instead of the expected `2.66`. This changes the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. No other behavior changes.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-pr"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The nightly build failure is fixed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, though its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding. That made `2.665` round to `2.67` instead of `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/banker-rounding-fin-212`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner, so that still has to happen through the normal review process.", "type": "text"}]}]}